            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0429" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115 Standard Vacuum Oil Company/43:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-01T16:00:00+08:00">August 1, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 1—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>329. Peiping’s 478, July 31, noon. I believe it would be advisable to authorize
                    the placing of a marine guard on the British tug as it appears that unless this
                    is done the American cargo in question will be unable to reach Tientsin.</p>
                <p>I presume Department will issue appropriate instructions to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
